WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.158 --> 00:00:03.158
(suspenseful music)

00:00:04.715 --> 00:00:06.928
- [Narrator] It's a
surprisingly dangerous mission,

00:00:06.928 --> 00:00:09.011
safely navigate the
skies of one of the most

00:00:09.011 --> 00:00:11.398
iconic tourist destinations in America.

00:00:11.398 --> 00:00:13.352
(rushing water)

00:00:13.352 --> 00:00:15.653
The helicopter pilots of Niagara Falls

00:00:15.653 --> 00:00:19.219
battle extreme wind and
unpredictable weather conditions,

00:00:19.219 --> 00:00:22.860
all to give tourists that
one spectacular view.

00:00:22.860 --> 00:00:24.718
- [Stanley] Sometimes it is very scary.

00:00:24.718 --> 00:00:27.215
You try not to let the fear over come you,

00:00:27.215 --> 00:00:29.306
so you can control the aircraft,

00:00:29.306 --> 00:00:31.147
you get it back to a safe environment,

00:00:31.147 --> 00:00:32.464
so you can go home at night.

00:00:32.464 --> 00:00:33.952
That's the name of the game, go home.

00:00:33.952 --> 00:00:36.035
(laughs)

00:00:43.686 --> 00:00:46.353
(water flowing)

00:00:48.544 --> 00:00:51.021
(upbeat music)

00:00:51.021 --> 00:00:52.526
My name is Stanley Snopkowski.

00:00:52.526 --> 00:00:55.325
I've been flying over
Niagara Falls about 20 years.

00:00:55.325 --> 00:00:57.573
And each day is different.

00:00:57.573 --> 00:00:59.566
I spent 20 years in the military.

00:00:59.566 --> 00:01:02.819
I've flown in Germany, England, Vietnam,

00:01:02.819 --> 00:01:07.780
and the weather here is
nothing like anything else.

00:01:07.780 --> 00:01:10.834
(intensifying string music)

00:01:10.834 --> 00:01:14.001
(helicopter whirring)

00:01:23.623 --> 00:01:25.063
Niagara Falls is beautiful.

00:01:25.063 --> 00:01:26.472
But like anything beautiful,

00:01:26.472 --> 00:01:28.383
there's a ugly side to it.

00:01:28.383 --> 00:01:30.463
The weather here can change quite rapidly.

00:01:30.463 --> 00:01:33.431
You can have snow showers,
and five minutes later,

00:01:33.431 --> 00:01:35.465
you can have bright sunny blue skies.

00:01:35.465 --> 00:01:36.936
You have to have a healthy respect for it,

00:01:36.936 --> 00:01:39.944
because it can go wrong
in a matter of minutes.

00:01:39.944 --> 00:01:43.694
The winds can gust up to
30 to 40 miles an hour.

00:01:43.694 --> 00:01:45.509
When the wind comes around the buildings,

00:01:45.509 --> 00:01:48.269
it tends to create mechanical turbulence,

00:01:48.269 --> 00:01:51.605
either an updraft or a
downdraft, or swirling.

00:01:51.605 --> 00:01:53.213
And then sometimes when you make the turn

00:01:53.213 --> 00:01:55.134
into the wind, it's almost sometimes like

00:01:55.134 --> 00:01:56.405
hitting a brick wall.

00:01:56.405 --> 00:01:59.117
I've had instances where
the aircraft wanted

00:01:59.117 --> 00:02:00.509
to come apart, quit flying.

00:02:00.509 --> 00:02:01.958
And we nursed it down to the ground.

00:02:01.958 --> 00:02:03.438
We got down and we and walked away.

00:02:03.438 --> 00:02:05.241
And it could have ended up differently,

00:02:05.241 --> 00:02:07.428
without the training,
without the knowledge.

00:02:07.428 --> 00:02:09.756
(laughs)

00:02:09.756 --> 00:02:12.748
I sometimes think that Mother
Nature's not my friend today,

00:02:12.748 --> 00:02:15.284
because of the winds or
because of the rain or snow.

00:02:15.284 --> 00:02:16.340
You deal with that,

00:02:16.340 --> 00:02:17.725
and hopefully come out on the good end.

00:02:17.725 --> 00:02:19.172
Or the other thing is, is you just sit there

00:02:19.172 --> 00:02:21.099
and you say, okay, you win today.

00:02:21.099 --> 00:02:22.043
I'm not going to fly.

00:02:22.043 --> 00:02:24.459
(laughs)

00:02:24.459 --> 00:02:29.268
I look at the falls and I
see the beauty of nature.

00:02:29.268 --> 00:02:33.076
Some days, after a major
storm comes through,

00:02:33.076 --> 00:02:35.325
the air is so clear.

00:02:35.325 --> 00:02:39.060
You have maybe 100 miles visibility.

00:02:39.060 --> 00:02:42.124
And it's just awe inspiring
to be able to see all that,

00:02:42.124 --> 00:02:44.622
and, uh, see the falls from a different angle.

00:02:44.622 --> 00:02:45.872
I just love it.

